# Product-origin routing, served by Cloudflare Workers static assets with NO Worker
# script (wrangler.jsonc has no `main`). Requests matched here or by a static asset
# are free and never count against the Workers request quota.
#
# Model (backstage ADR 0001):
#   /                         -> landing home (dist/landing.html, rule below)
#   any path with a file      -> that file (/en/*, /ru/*, robots.txt, chunks, ...)
#   any other path            -> Angular SPA shell (dist/index.html), 200, URL
#                                kept: assets.not_found_handling =
#                                "single-page-application". No app-route list,
#                                no reserved-locale list to keep in sync.
#
# Rules are first-match and are evaluated BEFORE assets, so never add a splat
# that could shadow a landing or app file.
#
# `/` rewrites to `/landing`, not `/landing.html`: the latter answers 307 under
# html_handling. The rule is exact (no splat), and a query string on `/` still
# matches it.
#
# www -> apex is a zone Redirect Rule, not this file (see docs/HOSTING.md).

# --- Landing home -------------------------------------------------------------
# The root index.html is the app shell (the SPA fallback); the landing owns /.
# The rewrite target is not re-matched, so /landing can 301 home without a loop:
# the landing has one public URL, `/` (its canonical).
/               /landing                              200
/landing        /                                     301

# --- Permanent redirects ------------------------------------------------------
# English is the default locale and owns the bare root.
/en             /                                     301
/en/            /                                     301
# Legacy /pwa/* -> root-mounted route. Remove once no old /pwa/* links remain.
/pwa            /                                     301
/pwa/*          /:splat                               301
# Unprefixed legal pages -> the default locale's copy.
/privacy        /en/privacy                           301
/privacy/       /en/privacy                           301
/terms          /en/terms                             301
/terms/         /en/terms                             301
